+
+## AI Provider Fabric architecture law
+
+- Browser code never calls Gemini, Groq, Mistral, Cohere, OpenRouter, SambaNova, NVIDIA, or Workers AI directly.
+- Provider secrets exist only as relay-side environment/secrets and never enter canonical or portable state.
+- Use small native-`fetch` adapters; do not add provider SDKs merely for HTTP normalization.
+- Route by capability, privacy, verified-free eligibility, quota, health, and lifecycle.
+- `allowPaid=false`; unknown free status blocks.
+- Youth-sensitive, financial-sensitive, secret, and unapproved work-internal packets are rejected before transport.
+- AI output remains a proposal with provider/model/prompt/packet provenance.
+- Deterministic Today, Promise Radar, WIP, proof, migration, merge, and recovery remain non-AI contracts.
+- Free-provider failure or quota exhaustion must leave complete local/manual functionality.
+- Continuous evaluation uses synthetic Kevin-shaped fixtures and cannot silently change an active route.
+
+# Disk-as-memory control system
+
+The repository is your persistent brain.
+
+At mission start, use and maintain:
+
+- `ACTIVE_MISSION.md`
+- `docs/evolution/2026-08-12-kevin-personalization-ai-fabric-v40/MISSION_STATE.json`
+- `06_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md`
+- `PROGRESS.md`
+- `ASSUMPTIONS.md`
+- `DECISIONS.md`
+- `EVIDENCE_INDEX.md`
+
+Before each wave:
+
+1. read the current mission state;
+2. identify the next unchecked dependency-ready task;
+3. update the current wave/task;
+4. state the expected proof;
+5. make the smallest coherent implementation slice.
+
+After each coherent slice:
+
+1. run focused tests;
+2. record exact commands and exit codes;
+3. inspect the diff;
+4. update the ledger;
+5. update evidence;
+6. update progress;
+7. create a reversible checkpoint;
+8. continue automatically.
+
+Before context becomes crowded:
+
+- compact facts into the mission files;
+- record exact current code state;
+- record every modified file;
+- record the last passing commands;
+- record the next unchecked task;
+- do not spend the remaining context writing a broad summary;
+- keep implementing while tools remain available.
+
+One writer owns `index.html` at a time. Other agents may inspect, design tests, research, or review non-overlapping files, but no simultaneous app writers are allowed.
