+# FINAL_KEVINOS_V40_HANDOFF
+
+## 1. Executive result
+
+State what shipped, what Kevin can now do, and the honest completion/activation status.
+
+## 2. Baseline and final versions
+
+- starting/final app, schema, cache;
+- workspace Git status;
+- remote actions performed (normally none);
+- preactivation and final gate results.
+
+## 3. Kevin-shaped product evolution
+
+Cover Role Registry, commitments, Project Spine, Resume Capsules, Today, WIP/Review, playbooks/onboarding, AI Studio, privacy, search, and supporting workflows.
+
+## 4. AI Provider Fabric
+
+- canonical capability/request/result/error/usage contracts;
+- adapter registry and exact aliases/models;
+- privacy classification/redaction/denial;
+- zero-dollar eligibility, quotas, circuits, and fallback;
+- provenance and content-free receipts;
+- Provider Control Center;
+- synthetic golden lab and human promotion/rollback;
+- all-provider-disabled behavior.
+
+## 5. Provider activation status
+
+For each core and optional provider state only redacted facts: `VERIFIED_FREE_ACTIVE`, `CONFIGURED_DISABLED`, `OPTIONAL_MISSING`, `ACCOUNT_OR_REGION_BLOCKED`, `FREE_ELIGIBILITY_BLOCKED`, or `REVOKED`. Include the exact model and date verified where allowed. Never include keys, prompt/response content, or secret hashes.
+
+## 6. Credentials-last ceremony and secret proof
+
+Confirm K-1–K9 and preactivation completed before the request; Kevin was told not to paste keys into chat; silent ignored local entry was used; permissions/ignore/rotation/revoke checks passed; no key entered source, app state, export, sync, logs, patches, screenshots, output, or hashes.
+
+## 7. State and migration contract
+
+Canonical additions, normalizers, v39→v40 phases, fingerprints, snapshots, remap behavior, rollback, import/merge/convergence, and provider-secret exclusion.
+
+## 8. Acceptance map
+
+Map every acceptance ID to PASS evidence, narrowly documented BLOCKED-EXTERNAL, or explicitly authorized WAIVED.
+
+## 9. Tests and commands
+
+Exact commands, exit codes, UTC dates, and redacted log paths.
+
+## 10. Browser, accessibility, offline, and performance evidence
+
+Required widths, console, overflow, keyboard/focus, reduced motion, touch targets, offline/reload, zero-provider state, and representative-scale observations.
+
+## 11. Privacy and security proof
+
+Privacy monotonicity, youth-sensitive default, AI manifest, person-note opt-in, public-output redaction, pre-transport denials with zero calls, XSS, connection exclusion, hard free-only policy, no direct browser providers, and secret scans.
+
+## 12. Files changed
+
+Group source, relay, tests, fixtures, docs, evidence, and tooling.
+
+## 13. Assumptions and decisions
+
+List IDs and revisit triggers.
+
+## 14. Residual risks and external/manual gates
+
+Be exact. Missing optional keys are honest disabled lanes. Difficult local work is not external.
+
+## 15. Remote actions deliberately not performed
+
+Confirm no push, PR, merge, tag, deploy, publish, send, calendar create, financial action, billing change, remote secret mutation, data deletion, or GATE-76 bypass unless separately authorized and evidenced.
+
+## 16. Patch, checksums, and rollback
+
+Paths and exact safe use instructions, including provider alias/prompt/policy rollback and key rotation/revocation.
+
+## 17. Kevin's next physical action
+
+One concrete safe action to review/use the result.
